      "id": 1,
      "text": "Burns City began as Keck's Church in 1849, founded by early settler Christian Keck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burns_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1849 as Keck's Church, renamed Burns City in 1890, and closed in 1957.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burns_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name came from a railroad engineer whose wife’s maiden name was Burns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burns_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Burns City sits on a ridge that drains north into First Creek and south into Seed Tick Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
